# Allowlist model: ignore EVERYTHING, then un-ignore only what the
# repo-root-context build (the runtime image via
# deploy/docker/runtime.Dockerfile) actually COPIES. This keeps the build
# context to a few MB of source instead of the whole tree (target/ alone is many
# GB), and it stays correct when new heavy dirs appear (they are ignored by
# default, never dragged in). The builder base does NOT build from the repo
# root: it uses the staged `.weft-base-context/` dir as its own context.
#
# The runtime Dockerfile COPIES: rust-toolchain.toml, Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock, crates/, catalog/ and the builder base's recipe under
# deploy/docker/. deploy/ is kept so the Dockerfile referenced with `-f`
# is inside the context too.
#
# SYNC: what the repo-root build context ships <-> the runtime image hash
#       inputs in crates/weft-cli/src/images.rs (NOT_IN_THE_BINARY +
#       weft_catalog::is_node_tree_excluded, which every hash walk
#       applies): a path that changes what a
#       binary compiles TO must be covered by both, or two trees with
#       one hash build different images.
*

!rust-toolchain.toml
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!deploy/
# The runtime image carries the standard library a version compiles
# against (deploy/docker/runtime.Dockerfile).
!catalog/

# Even inside the allowlisted dirs, never ship build artifacts or VCS/dev junk.
# SYNC: this block <-> crates/weft-catalog/src/lib.rs (NODE_TREE_EXCLUDE +
#       NODE_TREE_EXCLUDE_SUFFIXES). Every hash walk and staging copy
#       leaves out exactly those names, so the CLI hashing the checkout
#       and a dispatcher hashing the runtime image's copy agree.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.svelte-kit/
**/.git/
**/.weft/
**/.env
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
